      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "The user in question has been renamed to not be a zero length string. Santisation is much stricter now compared to back when the account was created in 2017 (with a bug making it an empty string rather than spaces later on) so any new accounts should not be able to have an empty string as a display name. I'll confirm with our API team to ensure there's no other empty string users that have somehow been created",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-06-28T13:59:28.964Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is currently at least one user on VRChat who has an empty string as a display name, which is breaking worlds and leading to unexpected behavior. Their profile description reflects that issue as well.\nWhile most people aren't even aware of that, others need to carefully add extra code everywhere, leading to additional performance cost for all other users which should ideally be avoided. \nI assume this is a result of VRChat deciding to trim invisible characters from display names and it was simply an oversight, not the intention of that user, but instead of adding extra code everywhere now, the only proper solution is to rename this one user instead and ensure that no other VRChat user has an empty string as a display name ever.",
